EXTENSION "ArM5_Guardians_of_the_Forests_TheBlackForest_SchadritMagaExMiscellanea" {
    NAME "Ars Magica Fifth Edition, Guardians of the Forests - Schadrit, maga Ex Miscellanea"
    VERSION "0.5.0"
    SPEC_VERSION "0.5"
    RELEASE_DATE "2026-10-06"
    DEPENDS_ON "ArM5_Guardians_of_the_Forests_Core_Ext"

    # Schadrit, maga Ex Miscellanea (Chapter Six: The Black Forest, p63): one character, its printed stat lines verbatim fields, its write-up the DESCRIPTION.

    #td98130636e531077c6906d ^"Schadrit, maga Ex Miscellanea" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tHoHTL05ExampleCharacterAA ^"Example Character"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Role" STRING "Magus"
            ^"Covenant" LIST [#t6cb750c26a1c05850985ea ^"Dankmar"]
            ^"Age" STRING "approximately 160 (Master)"
            ^"Personality Traits" STRING "Malicious +5, Vengeful +4, Callous +3"
            ^"Source" STRING "Guardians of the Forests"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 63
        }
        DESCRIPTION "Schadrit is a former apprentice of House Bonisagus and a former resident of Durenmar. When Aschlaranda of Bonisagus reappeared at Durenmar (see Chapter 3: Tribunal History and Customs, The Schism War), she brought Schadrit with her, and she completed her apprenticeship at Durenmar. When Aschlaranda was cast out from House Bonisagus, Schadrit was only a year away from her Gauntlet, but she was forced to suffer the same fate as her mistress. Together they founded a covenant, naming it Dankmar in parody of the birthplace of the Order. Schadrit is truly ancient, only a few decades from completing her second century. Her longevity potion has not preserved her looks as well as it has her age, and she is a withered hag who keeps herself shrouded in a voluminous black robe with a deep hood. Her face is so seamed with wrinkles that her features are barely discernible, except for her long, mole-covered nose. Schadrit has developed an expertise in Faerie Magic, and is perhaps the only practitioner outside of House Merinita. She is malicious to the point of downright evil, and rules Dankmar with an iron hand."
    }

}
